{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "fdbd28d5-85db-44b7-980e-d7531411fa41"/*GestureRecognitionExample*/,
  "Description": "Recognizes hand gestures in a live camera image and shows the built-in debug view: the camera frame with the detected hand landmarks.\n\nThe recognized gesture is provided as data: [PrimaryGesture] is the name of the recognized basic gesture (None, Fist, Open Palm, Point, Peace, Thumbs Up) - connect it to a string input or compare it to trigger things - and [Confidence] a fixed value per gesture type, not a recognizer score. [PointBuffer] holds the 21 hand landmarks per hand like [HandLandmarkDetectionExample], [HandCount] the number of hands.\n\nShow a clear hand to the camera; the gesture rules run on top of hand landmark detection, so hands need to be reasonably visible.",
  "InputUis": [],
  "SymbolChildUis": [
    {
      "ChildId": "027a4a31-50b5-4d93-a876-e0f5adbcb3b3",
